1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:04,800
90 minutes gone… and Manchester United were losing the Champions League final.

2
00:00:04,850 --> 00:00:07,750
Bayern Munich had scored in the 6th minute, from a free kick.

3
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:10,700
For more than 80 minutes, United couldn’t find a way back.

4
00:00:10,750 --> 00:00:12,900
The referee showed 3 minutes of added time.

5
00:00:12,950 --> 00:00:15,900
Bayern’s ribbons were already being tied to the trophy.

6
00:00:15,950 --> 00:00:18,700
The UEFA president left his seat to go and present it.

7
00:00:18,750 --> 00:00:24,600
91 minutes. A corner… and even the goalkeeper, Peter Schmeichel, runs up into the box.

8
00:00:24,650 --> 00:00:27,800
The ball breaks to Teddy Sheringham… 1–1.

9
00:00:27,850 --> 00:00:31,600
Barely 2 minutes later… another corner. Sheringham flicks it on…

10
00:00:31,650 --> 00:00:35,050
…and Ole Gunnar Solskjær pokes it into the roof of the net. 2–1.

11
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:36,950
Bayern’s players collapsed on the grass.

12
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:41,450
United had won their first European Cup in 31 years… and the treble.

13
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:45,850
Greatest finish to a final? Or can you name a better one?
